WEBVTT

00:01.790 --> 00:04.250
The leader of the winged knights, Edil,

00:04.250 --> 00:06.630
turns out to be an old friend of Helck's.

00:06.630 --> 00:09.170
Edil reveals the reason
that humans have sprouted wings

00:09.170 --> 00:12.170
is because they've awakened as heroes.

00:12.500 --> 00:14.170
After Hyura defeats him in battle,

00:14.170 --> 00:16.500
Edil is promptly killed
by one of his own comrades.

00:16.500 --> 00:19.080
Meanwhile, Helck and Vermilio

00:19.080 --> 00:23.750
get sucked up into a gate
that was hidden below the castle.

00:49.420 --> 00:51.670
A crazed cog in the machine

00:51.670 --> 00:54.330
Lets loose a shrill cry

00:54.330 --> 00:56.330
Destined for battle and foaming at the mouth

00:56.330 --> 00:59.170
As if waiting for an opening

00:59.420 --> 01:01.500
I got dealt a dangerous card

01:01.500 --> 01:04.170
But prediciments are opportunities

01:04.170 --> 01:06.080
There's no way in hell I'm giving up

01:06.080 --> 01:08.960
The last one standing is the winner

01:09.170 --> 01:11.330
Let's just dance hand in hand

01:11.330 --> 01:14.080
With the grinning devil

01:14.080 --> 01:16.330
No need to care about appearances

01:16.330 --> 01:18.670
Courage trembles with fury

01:18.670 --> 01:21.630
Before the darkness can consume it all

01:21.830 --> 01:22.500
Break it

01:22.500 --> 01:24.000
Kick it away

01:24.000 --> 01:27.080
It's your common sense that'll be smashed to bits

01:27.080 --> 01:31.580
Ignite a flame in the soul that no one can extinguish

01:31.880 --> 01:37.290
This prayer that I now offer to the endless world

01:37.290 --> 01:42.040
Will never stop until the day comes when it gets answered

01:42.040 --> 01:43.670
Always burning

01:43.670 --> 01:46.580
It's my soul

01:54.040 --> 01:58.960
<b>The Remote Island Village</b>

01:59.330 --> 02:00.540
Lord Azudra!

02:00.540 --> 02:02.210
A-awful news about Lady Vermilio!

02:02.210 --> 02:03.290
What happened?!

02:03.670 --> 02:07.290
Lady Vermilio has gone missing
after being sucked into a gate?!

02:07.290 --> 02:08.630
This can't be happening...

02:09.210 --> 02:12.380
No, stop it. Don't start going into panic mode.

02:12.380 --> 02:16.040
The most important thing that you can do
in times like these is keep your cool.

02:16.580 --> 02:20.040
Ve-Ve-Ver-Ver-Ver-Vermi...

02:20.040 --> 02:23.580
It's... my fault... that Ver-Vermi...

02:23.580 --> 02:27.170
Please get a hold of yourself, Lord Azudra!

02:39.420 --> 02:42.460
I know what this is... it's the ocean!

02:42.460 --> 02:44.500
I saw it just once when I was very young.

02:45.290 --> 02:48.130
So, we've been flung all the way
to the edge of the continent.

02:58.040 --> 03:00.750
There's no toxin here whatsoever, huh?

03:01.250 --> 03:04.460
It's incredible just how comfortable it feels
being in a land free of toxin...

03:05.130 --> 03:06.920
I had completely forgotten.

03:11.630 --> 03:15.630
I wonder how long it will take me
to return to the Empire.

03:16.080 --> 03:18.000
I need to get back as soon as I can.

03:18.880 --> 03:23.330
In any case, I'm glad that gate
sent me to such an abundant land.

03:23.330 --> 03:24.790
If this had been barren wilderness,

03:24.790 --> 03:27.880
then I would've died of starvation
even without the toxin to worry about.

03:30.710 --> 03:32.750
This rhythmical sound in the air...

03:32.750 --> 03:34.670
It's definitely not natural.

03:34.670 --> 03:36.420
Is somebody else here?

03:36.420 --> 03:39.040
Wait, what if it's Helck?

03:39.250 --> 03:40.380
Oh no!

03:40.380 --> 03:42.420
That means this really is his crummy cape!

03:45.670 --> 03:47.630
But it doesn't smell bad...

03:48.250 --> 03:50.170
Who cares about that right now!

03:50.170 --> 03:51.210
Damn Helck!

03:51.210 --> 03:53.580
What the hell is he getting up to now?!

03:55.580 --> 03:56.790
I'm close...

03:56.790 --> 03:58.580
I can't let my guard down.

03:58.580 --> 04:00.130
He's an enemy.

04:03.210 --> 04:04.380
Found him.

04:04.790 --> 04:06.920
But what's he doing over there?

04:07.170 --> 04:10.460
No way! Did he build that house?!

04:10.460 --> 04:14.210
I knew he was talented,
but this is a new level of handy...

04:19.130 --> 04:21.670
Uh, what am I looking at here?

04:21.670 --> 04:23.290
Hello there!

04:26.420 --> 04:29.040
H-HELLO THERE!

04:29.040 --> 04:30.920
Um, hi.

04:30.920 --> 04:33.420
I heard you the first time,
so could you keep it down a little?

04:35.920 --> 04:38.420
Hey! Good to see that you're awake!

04:38.420 --> 04:40.830
D-don't scare me like that, fool!

04:40.830 --> 04:41.830
Sorry, my bad.

04:42.170 --> 04:43.710
I can't believe I slipped up like that!

04:43.710 --> 04:46.500
I'm such a fool!
He could have killed me just now!

04:46.670 --> 04:50.130
A-are we going to fight? Right here?

04:50.130 --> 04:51.670
I see you finished the house!

04:51.670 --> 04:52.580
Yep!

04:52.580 --> 04:54.790
I couldn't have done
it without you guys to help!

04:54.790 --> 04:55.500
Thank you so muc-

04:55.500 --> 04:56.880
You're very welcome!

04:57.040 --> 04:59.580
Wh-why would you go and build a house?

04:59.580 --> 05:00.960
Are you kidding?

05:00.960 --> 05:04.290
Because sleeping in a house is much better
than spending the night outdoors.

05:04.290 --> 05:06.040
I mean, it could rain or worse!

05:06.040 --> 05:06.830
It will rain!

05:07.630 --> 05:09.920
How long are you planning to stay here?

05:09.920 --> 05:12.500
Is this going to be your new home or what?

05:12.500 --> 05:13.830
Heavens no!

05:13.830 --> 05:16.170
But it doesn't seem like
we can go back anytime soon.

05:16.170 --> 05:18.500
So I decided to make a base of operations.

05:18.500 --> 05:22.130
What do you mean we can't go back?
Explain yourself.

05:22.130 --> 05:24.500
Well, this is some kind of island.

05:24.500 --> 05:28.210
Which means walking back
to where we came from isn't an option.

05:28.210 --> 05:32.330
Th-this is an island?!
We're not on the edge of the continent?!

05:32.330 --> 05:35.380
I was able to loop around the entire place
in just a few minutes, so I'm positive.

05:35.380 --> 05:36.830
This is Remote Island!

05:36.830 --> 05:41.290
We really ended up in the last place
anyone would expect.

05:41.790 --> 05:44.170
Y-you've gotta be kidding!

05:44.170 --> 05:46.380
But hey, at least it's a nice place!

05:46.380 --> 05:47.580
I love it!

05:47.580 --> 05:48.830
Y-you fool!

05:48.830 --> 05:50.960
Quit being so damn carefree!

05:52.710 --> 05:55.540
There has to be way
for us to get back, right?

06:00.380 --> 06:02.920
Yikes! Here comes the rain!

06:02.920 --> 06:04.630
Take cover in the house!

06:08.920 --> 06:13.790
On the bright side, I guess the Empire
is free from the threat of Helck now...

06:14.040 --> 06:16.290
Hey! What are you doing?

06:17.170 --> 06:20.000
I'm sure as hell not going into a house
the enemy built!

06:21.790 --> 06:22.460
Oh cra-!

06:24.500 --> 06:26.920
What are you doing?!
Put me down!

06:31.630 --> 06:32.920
Whew! Safe!

06:32.920 --> 06:34.580
Out! I call out!

06:35.170 --> 06:38.330
D-dammit! Just mind your own business!

06:38.330 --> 06:39.330
Anne.

06:40.130 --> 06:41.080
It's all right!

06:41.080 --> 06:42.290
What is?!

06:42.630 --> 06:45.540
This place is chock-full of good quality trees!

06:45.540 --> 06:49.170
We can use them to build a sturdy boat
and that will be our ticket across the ocean!

06:49.380 --> 06:52.130
Let's join forces to get back
to the Demon Realm!

06:52.130 --> 06:54.540
It's all right! We will make it there!

06:54.540 --> 06:57.080
So don't give up until the very end!

06:57.080 --> 06:58.460
We're in this together!

06:58.460 --> 07:00.290
Uh, okay.

07:01.170 --> 07:02.920
Why the hell did I say "okay"?!

07:02.920 --> 07:05.630
This is the opposite of okay!
I can't let this guy return to the Demon Realm!

07:05.630 --> 07:07.920
Otherwise we'll be right back at square one!

07:07.920 --> 07:09.330
Don't look so down!

07:09.330 --> 07:11.000
Have hope!

07:11.000 --> 07:12.250
It cleared up!

07:12.250 --> 07:13.830
Wow! That was fast!

07:14.130 --> 07:16.130
Actually, now that I think about it,

07:16.130 --> 07:20.670
this big lummox did actually try to save me
when I was getting sucked into the gate.

07:21.080 --> 07:24.960
And it would have been easy for him
to just run away from it instead...

07:24.960 --> 07:27.000
So why come after me?

07:27.670 --> 07:30.000
Not to mention,
the entire time we've been here...

07:30.000 --> 07:33.290
he's had plenty of opportunities
to kill me but hasn't.

07:33.290 --> 07:34.580
Alrighty!

07:34.580 --> 07:37.380
I'm hungry. Let's go look for some food!

07:37.380 --> 07:38.880
I'm gonna head out.

07:39.330 --> 07:42.670
Are you actually our ally, Helck?

07:50.250 --> 07:53.670
I had surmised the winged knights
were in fact humans,

07:53.670 --> 07:56.380
but not that they had awakened as heroes.

07:56.790 --> 07:59.330
And a spatial-teleportation spell, eh?

07:59.330 --> 08:02.500
That explains why they
weren't taking any further action.

08:04.290 --> 08:05.710
How curious.

08:05.710 --> 08:09.210
It's abnormal for their magic capabilities
to grow this drastically.

08:09.210 --> 08:11.380
Not to mention the "hero awakening"...

08:11.380 --> 08:13.750
I've never heard of such a spell.

08:14.250 --> 08:18.000
Was a genius spellcaster born in the human realm?
Or is it something else?

08:18.000 --> 08:20.080
Um, if I may, Lord Azudra...

08:20.080 --> 08:21.380
Now that you've calmed down,

08:21.380 --> 08:24.130
will you please tell us
what the plan is moving forward?

08:25.290 --> 08:28.580
As if you even need to ask.
This is a race against time.

08:28.580 --> 08:31.580
If the humans manage
to fully mature into heroes,

08:31.580 --> 08:34.000
then they will be too much for us to handle.

08:34.000 --> 08:36.130
Okay, so like I figured...

08:36.380 --> 08:37.580
Yes.

08:37.580 --> 08:39.750
We send a search party out for Vermikins.

08:39.750 --> 08:41.000
Huh?

08:41.000 --> 08:42.580
But based on what you said,

08:42.580 --> 08:45.540
it seemed like the next step
was launching an attack on the human realm...

08:45.540 --> 08:46.540
Have you lost your mind?!

08:46.540 --> 08:49.040
There's no way in hell
that I can fight anybody right now

08:49.040 --> 08:51.040
because I'm worried SICK about Vermikins!

08:51.040 --> 08:52.540
I'm a mental health wreck!

08:52.540 --> 08:54.580
If we want any chance
at beating the humans,

08:54.580 --> 08:58.130
then we need to find Vermikins
and bring her back ASAP!

08:58.420 --> 08:59.710
Yes, but sir,

08:59.710 --> 09:02.830
many of our troops have been deployed
to either protect the north border

09:02.830 --> 09:04.630
or on monster slaying missions.

09:04.630 --> 09:08.460
And if you consider that a confrontation
with the humans lies on the horizon...

09:08.460 --> 09:11.330
I think it will be nearly impossible
to organize a search party

09:11.330 --> 09:13.210
large enough to get the job done.

09:13.210 --> 09:15.130
I mean, this continent is so huge.

09:15.130 --> 09:18.710
Who knows how many years it could take
just to find Lady Vermilio?

09:20.080 --> 09:22.830
We don't need a large search party.

09:22.830 --> 09:23.790
Huh?

09:24.040 --> 09:26.580
Because we're going to use a locator spell.

09:27.210 --> 09:28.880
And what is that?

09:28.880 --> 09:31.130
It's a spell that was created
as a safety measure

09:31.130 --> 09:34.130
when sending someone
into unexplored territory.

09:34.130 --> 09:36.790
It will allow us to roughly track her position.

09:36.790 --> 09:37.960
H-how incredible!

09:37.960 --> 09:39.830
There's just nothing that you can't do, huh?

09:39.830 --> 09:41.460
Hold on, Lord Azudra.

09:41.460 --> 09:45.420
I'm fairly certain that spell requires you to have
a physical piece of the person you want to track.

09:45.670 --> 09:48.670
We don't have any of
Lady Vermilio's fingernails or hair-

09:50.540 --> 09:54.460
Turns out Vermikins getting a haircut
just before leaving was a stroke of luck.

09:54.460 --> 09:57.290
You can't be serious, Lord Azudra.

09:57.290 --> 09:59.920
Are you saying that you kept a lock
of Lady Vermilio's hair?!

10:01.080 --> 10:04.080
Whoa, hold your horses.
Don't treat me like some kind of perv.

10:04.080 --> 10:05.790
I don't have any of her hair.

10:05.790 --> 10:07.380
Although I did try to take some...

10:08.750 --> 10:09.420
OH GOD!

10:09.420 --> 10:10.460
OH GOD!
I got lit on fire as it was burned away.<b></b>

10:10.460 --> 10:11.460
I got lit on fire as it was burned away.

10:11.460 --> 10:13.790
So you're not denying you tried to take some.

10:13.790 --> 10:15.330
But then who does have it?

10:16.170 --> 10:17.920
I have some with me.

10:18.330 --> 10:19.460
Where I come from,

10:19.460 --> 10:21.960
when someone we care about
leaves on a journey far away,

10:21.960 --> 10:25.080
we have a custom of caring for
a small bundle of their hair in the belief

10:25.080 --> 10:27.500
that it will help keep them safe.

10:27.670 --> 10:29.500
Would this help with the spell?

10:29.960 --> 10:32.670
You never cease to amaze, Ms. Ista!
How fantastic!

10:32.670 --> 10:35.420
So I get insults while Istykins gets praise?

10:35.420 --> 10:36.580
Whatever.

10:36.580 --> 10:38.290
Let's put the locator spell into action.

10:38.290 --> 10:40.670
Hon! Prepare me a map and wooden figure!

10:40.670 --> 10:41.710
Right away.

10:42.380 --> 10:45.580
I just put Vermikins hair
inside the wooden figure.

10:46.130 --> 10:48.000
And then activate the spell.

10:49.210 --> 10:51.830
This will cause the figure
to move across the map,

10:51.830 --> 10:53.830
and the place where it stops...

10:54.880 --> 10:57.290
That's where Vermikins is!

11:02.130 --> 11:03.500
WHERE THE HELL?!

11:03.500 --> 11:05.380
That's not even on the map!

11:05.380 --> 11:09.040
Uh... well, maybe she got sent
all the way off the continent...

11:09.040 --> 11:09.790
Huh?!

11:09.790 --> 11:11.960
Wh-what do we do now?

11:12.170 --> 11:13.540
I have no idea.

11:13.880 --> 11:15.000
HUH?!

11:19.380 --> 11:21.170
Hey, Asta, did you hear me?

11:21.170 --> 11:22.250
Yeah, I did.

11:22.250 --> 11:24.710
That's the deal. We're counting on you.

11:24.710 --> 11:27.460
Just promise me that you definitely
won't go overboard this time, okay?

11:27.460 --> 11:29.330
Yeah, all right.

11:29.330 --> 11:31.250
I'll be in touch with you again later.

11:31.250 --> 11:32.460
Bye-bye.

11:33.960 --> 11:35.170
How about that...

11:35.540 --> 11:38.630
It turns out the winged knights
were human after all.

11:38.630 --> 11:41.290
That explains why there are so many of them.

11:42.960 --> 11:46.250
And what's more,
they're all apparently hero status.

11:46.250 --> 11:48.580
That's just insane. Horrifying, even!

11:49.080 --> 11:50.170
In any case,

11:50.170 --> 11:52.670
I'm positive that Lady Vermilio
will return eventually.

11:52.670 --> 11:53.920
And in the meantime,

11:53.920 --> 11:57.130
I have to gather as much useful information
as I can for when she's back in action!

11:57.130 --> 11:59.170
Okay. Time to go overboard!

11:59.380 --> 12:02.460
For the peace of the Empire!
Let's do this!

12:11.830 --> 12:14.460
Keep at it! You'll catch one soon!

12:15.130 --> 12:19.170
Oh, well... I wasn't sighing
because I haven't caught a fish.

12:19.170 --> 12:20.250
Keep at it!

12:20.250 --> 12:21.210
Chin up!

12:21.920 --> 12:22.960
Thanks...

12:25.540 --> 12:27.250
I don't know what to think.

12:27.420 --> 12:31.710
During the finals, Helck didn't even
raise a finger against the winged knights.

12:31.710 --> 12:34.330
In fact, he helped them
by getting in Hyura's way.

12:34.580 --> 12:37.500
So no matter how you look at it,
he's not on our side.

12:37.500 --> 12:41.250
However, all of his conduct thereafter
has made me uncertain...

12:41.250 --> 12:45.080
Why doesn't he kill me? Why save me?

12:45.630 --> 12:47.880
Is it because I'm useful to him?

12:47.880 --> 12:49.460
But how, exactly?

12:49.460 --> 12:51.500
Is he actually our ally?

12:51.500 --> 12:54.920
But it that's the case,
why did he protect the winged knights?

12:55.830 --> 12:56.750
Dammit!

12:57.710 --> 12:59.710
This is getting me absolutely nowhere!

12:59.710 --> 13:02.290
Keep it up! You'll catch one soon!

13:02.750 --> 13:05.250
Should I just ask Helck
about his true motives?

13:05.750 --> 13:09.290
No, that might be opening pandora's box...

13:12.880 --> 13:16.080
Because if he proves himself to be a threat,
then we'll have to fight!

13:18.130 --> 13:20.710
There's no way I can win that battle
and come out alive!

13:20.710 --> 13:24.460
And in the worst-case scenario,
I die without bringing him down!

13:24.460 --> 13:26.250
Then Helck just returns to the continent

13:26.250 --> 13:29.540
and the Empire will face
impending doom from him once again!

13:30.630 --> 13:33.080
Fortunately, we have Azudra on our side.
Hey, you've got a bite! You've got a bite!<b></b>

13:33.080 --> 13:34.290
Even though I hate his guts,
You've got a bite! Hey, you've got a bite!<b></b>

13:34.290 --> 13:35.960
he's the strongest of the Elite Lords
under the right conditions.
You've got a bite! Hey, you've got a bite!<b></b>

13:35.960 --> 13:36.920
he's the strongest of the Elite Lords
under the right conditions.
Hello, Annie? Are you listening?<b></b>

13:36.920 --> 13:38.290
So he can hold his own!
Hello, Annie? Are you listening?<b></b>

13:38.290 --> 13:38.960
As much as I HATE him!
Hello, Annie? Are you listening?<b></b>

13:38.960 --> 13:40.080
As much as I HATE him!
There's a fish! You've got a bite!<b></b>

13:40.080 --> 13:41.170
With that in mind,
Hey, pay attention!<b></b>

13:41.170 --> 13:41.790
perhaps buying time by leaving things
Hey, pay attention!<b></b>

13:41.790 --> 13:43.080
perhaps buying time by leaving things
Are you okay, Annie? I'm talking to you!<b></b>

13:43.080 --> 13:44.830
ambiguous like this is the safer choice...
Are you okay, Annie? I'm talking to you!<b></b>

13:44.830 --> 13:46.130
Are you okay, Annie? I'm talking to you!

13:46.130 --> 13:46.790
There's a fish!

13:46.790 --> 13:47.880
What should I do?
There's a fish!<b></b>

13:47.880 --> 13:49.500
You gotta pull it up!

13:49.500 --> 13:51.960
If you don't do it soon,
then the fish will get away!

13:51.960 --> 13:53.420
Cheep!

13:55.880 --> 13:57.250
This is one strong fish!

13:57.250 --> 13:59.330
You can't just play tug of war with it!

13:59.330 --> 14:00.750
The string will break!

14:00.750 --> 14:03.210
First make the fish tired,
and then pull it up!

14:03.210 --> 14:04.580
A-all right!

14:06.960 --> 14:07.880
What?!

14:07.880 --> 14:10.290
How the hell can such a small fish
have so much power?!

14:10.290 --> 14:12.420
Because plankton are
a nutrient-dense super food!

14:13.040 --> 14:14.920
Well, you messed with the wrong demon!

14:14.920 --> 14:17.540
For I am the Elite Lor-
Anne from Management!

14:17.540 --> 14:19.920
I would never lose to some stupid fish!

14:22.170 --> 14:25.080
G-guess I should have known better
than to try and rush it...

14:25.420 --> 14:28.460
I'm sorry. Please don't look at me like that!

14:29.830 --> 14:31.790
NEVER GIVE UP!

14:32.380 --> 14:33.630
Helck...

14:35.960 --> 14:38.130
Seriously? Helping me again?

14:43.250 --> 14:45.580
Anne! You're incredible!

14:45.580 --> 14:47.380
The fish that you caught...

14:49.170 --> 14:50.960
was a real big whopper!

14:52.500 --> 14:54.210
THAT'S NOT EVEN A FISH!

14:54.210 --> 14:56.920
What the hell is that?!
Where'd you get it from?!

14:56.920 --> 14:58.670
It was walking along the ocean floor!

14:58.670 --> 14:59.880
Yikes!

14:59.880 --> 15:01.960
That thing is poisonous, you know!

15:02.630 --> 15:03.670
I'm gonna head out.

15:03.670 --> 15:05.830
G'night! Be careful!

15:05.830 --> 15:06.750
Okay!

15:20.790 --> 15:23.290
I went over a bunch of things
in my head yesterday,

15:23.290 --> 15:26.130
but I fell asleep without
ever coming to a decision...

15:27.250 --> 15:29.960
I've no idea where he even got them from,

15:29.960 --> 15:32.830
but I have to admit these pajamas
are pretty darn comfortable.

15:34.830 --> 15:36.330
No problems with the trap I set, either.

15:38.000 --> 15:40.380
Regardless, I can't afford to get sloppy!

15:42.920 --> 15:44.000
Who's there?

15:44.250 --> 15:45.750
Maybe it's that fuzzball.

15:46.750 --> 15:48.210
Is Helck not around?

15:49.250 --> 15:51.000
Hold on! I'm opening it now.

15:52.460 --> 15:53.750
Wazzup!

15:54.630 --> 15:56.000
Who the devil are you?

15:56.000 --> 15:57.000
Um...

15:57.420 --> 16:00.670
I'm, like, the dude who's
gotta deliver your breakfast!

16:00.670 --> 16:02.000
Breakfast?

16:04.130 --> 16:05.920
Somebody's already eaten half of it...

16:05.920 --> 16:06.880
Sorry!

16:06.880 --> 16:08.830
I got a bad case of the munchies
on my way here!

16:08.830 --> 16:11.130
But I held myself back
and left some for you!

16:11.420 --> 16:14.250
Well, I never asked for breakfast,
so it doesn't really matter.

16:14.710 --> 16:16.790
You're welcome to eat the rest,
if you want.

16:17.130 --> 16:20.130
Tell me something.
Who prepared all of this?

16:20.290 --> 16:22.710
I can really have the rest?! Thanks, yo!

16:22.710 --> 16:25.580
Welp, Imma go home now. Peace out!

16:25.580 --> 16:27.330
Listen to what I'm saying!

16:27.540 --> 16:30.130
It wuz the village chief
who asked me to bring it!

16:30.130 --> 16:31.540
Chief?

16:31.540 --> 16:32.710
Interesting.

16:32.710 --> 16:34.790
So there is a village here after all.

16:35.040 --> 16:38.000
Helck must have borrowed
all these supplies from there.

16:38.000 --> 16:40.080
Welp, Imma leave now!

16:40.080 --> 16:41.210
Wait.

16:41.380 --> 16:43.330
I have a little favor to ask of you.

16:43.790 --> 16:44.880
Huh?

16:45.710 --> 16:47.170
Down there.

16:47.920 --> 16:49.880
Check it out, yo!

16:49.880 --> 16:51.630
You can see my house!

16:51.630 --> 16:53.330
How do we get down from here?

16:53.830 --> 16:56.580
Thatzzit! My house is right there!

16:56.580 --> 16:58.420
Yeah, looks like a nice house.

17:00.130 --> 17:01.790
Are there any other villages here?

17:01.790 --> 17:05.080
There are no villages.
Just a few houses and thatzzit.

17:05.210 --> 17:07.830
Are you the only ones
living on this island?

17:07.830 --> 17:11.080
Yezzur! It's just us.
We're the only ones around!

17:11.080 --> 17:14.670
Gee whiz, it's the first time in my life
I've seen somebody from outside the island!

17:14.670 --> 17:16.920
I'm, like, getting hyped up! Fo sho!

17:16.920 --> 17:18.210
Is that so?

17:18.210 --> 17:19.960
He's just like that fuzzball.

17:19.960 --> 17:22.080
They're not wary of strangers
around here, are they?

17:28.670 --> 17:31.380
Ya big nincompoop!
Whaddya bring her here for?!

17:31.630 --> 17:33.080
I take back what I said.

17:33.080 --> 17:36.080
It seems the village as a whole
is being pretty cautious towards us.

17:36.080 --> 17:37.710
Well, that's only natural.

17:37.710 --> 17:40.170
Aw shiz! I totally pooched it!

17:40.170 --> 17:42.330
Welp, Imma go get chewed out for a bit!

17:42.330 --> 17:44.920
So you're in trouble now?
Sorry about that.

17:47.080 --> 17:48.630
Annie!

17:50.290 --> 17:51.540
Good morning!

17:51.540 --> 17:52.630
Don't get so close!

17:52.630 --> 17:55.380
I absolutely hate when people
start clinging onto me!

17:55.750 --> 17:59.500
Oh, but this thing feels a lot softer
and fluffier than I thought...

17:59.500 --> 18:02.080
Gosh, Annie, you have
old lady smell on you.

18:02.580 --> 18:04.170
O-old lady?!

18:05.710 --> 18:07.330
Annie! Guess what?!

18:07.330 --> 18:08.630
Look, I'm not cool with nicknames-

18:08.630 --> 18:10.460
Helck said he's gonna make a boat!

18:10.460 --> 18:11.420
WHAT?!

18:11.580 --> 18:13.750
Where is he?! Where is Helck right now?!

18:13.750 --> 18:14.670
Over there!

18:16.540 --> 18:19.540
Oh no! He can't have figured out
the way back yet, can he?!

18:19.540 --> 18:20.460
This is bad!

18:20.460 --> 18:22.580
It hardly took him long
to build that house!

18:22.580 --> 18:24.960
Which means he can build a boat in no time!

18:24.960 --> 18:27.290
I cannot let him make it back
to the continent!

18:30.170 --> 18:31.330
Found him!

18:42.380 --> 18:44.710
Wh-what's that aura enveloping him?

18:46.290 --> 18:48.380
I'm sensing an incredible energy!

18:48.380 --> 18:51.830
Jeez! Just how far has he gone
to hide his true power level?!

18:57.130 --> 18:58.250
It just took wind pressure?!

19:00.500 --> 19:03.380
Whoa! The axe couldn't take all his strength
and broke into pieces!

19:03.380 --> 19:04.920
Has he never used one before or what?!

19:06.920 --> 19:09.750
Sucker! Now he can't make the boat!

19:14.580 --> 19:15.670
Goddammit!

19:15.670 --> 19:17.420
He always pulls shit like this!

19:18.380 --> 19:21.330
Eep! I'm such a fool!

19:21.630 --> 19:23.290
Cheep. Cheep.

19:24.040 --> 19:25.830
What do you think you're doing?

19:26.250 --> 19:27.540
I gotchu covered.

19:27.540 --> 19:30.750
I'm going to trick him into thinking
it was just a bird making some noise.

19:30.750 --> 19:31.500
Cheep!

19:31.500 --> 19:33.420
Cheep! Cheep! Cheep!

19:33.420 --> 19:36.040
Shucks! So it was you two I heard, huh?

19:38.170 --> 19:40.460
What brings you out here?

19:40.460 --> 19:42.580
I heard that you were building a boat.

19:42.580 --> 19:45.790
So, did you figure out which direction
will take us back home?

19:45.790 --> 19:47.540
Nope! Not yet.

19:47.540 --> 19:51.080
But I wanted to be prepared to
leave immediately once we do figure it out.

19:51.080 --> 19:53.500
Which is why I decided
to build the boat first.

19:53.920 --> 19:57.040
Oh. So you haven't
learned anything new, then.

19:57.040 --> 19:58.880
Don't look so depressed!

19:58.880 --> 20:00.500
It's only day two!

20:00.500 --> 20:02.500
Let's not rush and take it one thing at a time!

20:02.500 --> 20:03.210
Huh?

20:03.210 --> 20:05.130
Oh, sure...

20:30.290 --> 20:32.830
Are those... ruins?

20:32.830 --> 20:34.580
There are more of them all over the place.

20:34.580 --> 20:38.380
You know, this island might have been
very prosperous a long time ago.

20:38.380 --> 20:40.920
Did your ancestors build all these?

20:40.920 --> 20:42.130
I dunno!

20:42.540 --> 20:44.420
What a strange place...

20:44.420 --> 20:46.960
It feels nostalgic to me for some reason.

20:46.960 --> 20:48.540
Alrighty! It's finished!

20:48.540 --> 20:50.750
What? You already built the boat?!

20:53.830 --> 20:56.540
The quality of your work
is on the low end this time, huh...

20:57.210 --> 21:00.250
So, this is where you
wretched outsiders got off to.

21:01.250 --> 21:06.130
I've heard that you've been going 'round
and making a playground of our island.

21:07.460 --> 21:09.040
Come with me.

21:09.040 --> 21:11.420
We're gonna need to have a little chat.

21:19.830 --> 21:22.630
I promise you

21:22.630 --> 21:25.580
Someday when the world

21:25.580 --> 21:27.670
Comes to an end

21:27.670 --> 21:30.290
I hope we meet once again

21:42.380 --> 21:47.750
Someone once told me

21:47.750 --> 21:53.670
You were like a flower

21:53.670 --> 21:59.210
In a room without water, yet surely

21:59.210 --> 22:01.710
Blooming towards tomorrow

22:03.420 --> 22:06.210
If it was all a dream

22:06.210 --> 22:09.080
To know you

22:09.080 --> 22:12.000
To be in love

22:12.000 --> 22:15.500
I wouldn't know the meaning of life

22:16.330 --> 22:19.130
Even if tomorrow

22:19.130 --> 22:21.830
The rain pours

22:21.830 --> 22:24.210
Dawn will come and

22:24.210 --> 22:27.290
Rainbows will arch over the world

22:27.670 --> 22:30.380
The pain in my heart

22:30.380 --> 22:33.250
The tears trickling down

22:33.250 --> 22:36.710
Let's turn it into seeds for the future

22:36.710 --> 22:38.330
We go on

22:39.040 --> 22:41.080
Until our clumsy love

22:41.080 --> 22:44.250
Blooms into a flower

22:46.040 --> 22:50.830
<b>Next Episode</b>

22:46.040 --> 22:50.830
<b>Invasion</b>

22:46.830 --> 22:49.290
Next time: "Invasion"
